{
  "rationale": "The plant G models robot perception and motion in a grid world, including all controllable and uncontrollable events, with helper states for obstacle and blue-area recovery. The specification E enforces safety (obstacle avoidance, blue area escape), ensures move_backward is only used for front-obstacle recovery, prioritizes go_to_red for progress, and requires escape_blue immediately after blue_detected. Both automata are deterministic, with one controllable action per state except for perception/decision states. All uncontrollable events are total in every state.",
  "strategy": [
    "Use helper states for commit/recovery actions (e.g., forward_commit, rotate_commit_cw, recover_back, stuck, blue_escape_commit) to ensure one-shot controllable actions and safe transitions.",
    "Prioritize go_to_red when not in red area, escape_blue immediately after blue_detected, and use directed turns for obstacle recovery; move_backward is only reachable from front-obstacle recovery states."
  ],
